{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04I9", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$2$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b15315ec3c2fa7b154c0d17c24b63d47f12b572ea3fa602a460510e1a685b882", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:00948b344b400674f7ebc86397d3694abdc557b94bfab5dbb3768964cf34219c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis is a brief section concerning the notion of a <MATH_0001>-morphism\nof topoi.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d7880f280c5d7015fe275846feabbe6d7ae6f32a975a6582c6f13a7e8f390f64", "unit_id": "tag:04I9:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "04I9", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f, g : \\Sh(\\mathcal{C}) \\to \\Sh(\\mathcal{D})$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$g$", "MATH_0004": "$t : f_* \\to g_*$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-2-morphism-topoi}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e1d22b007787b1e1dc2d8c8dbaa396b6dc07ef3f20b9f79fcae95db7f0e96e13", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:047c2a5c211828406a8b6cda43e2d0037d28528d626a0e75b6cf93a35d5e2aa8", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>\nbe two morphisms of topoi. A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>2-morphism from <MATH_0002> to <MATH_0003><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nis given by a transformation of functors <MATH_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:19a9e39f13958c3d66d6bd7987ce10193008ab3922e79fbc4995a5656e8b3ac4", "unit_id": "tag:04IA:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "math_text_regions": [{"delimiter_kind": "display-dollar", "pieces": [{"kind": "locked", "placeholder": "MATHSEG_0001"}, {"kind": "text", "slot_id": "math/0001/text/0001"}, {"kind": "locked", "placeholder": "MATHSEG_0002"}], "region_id": "math/0001", "slots": [{"boundary_placeholders": ["MATHSEG_0001", "MATHSEG_0002"], "classification_witness": {"anchor": {"file": "sites.tex", "kind": "section", "matches": [{"command_byte_span": {"end": 316727, "start": 316718}, "command_hash": "sha256:3ddb92ccb3118de03d8d58e0e2b9a68498744d79e806286109a3f511be1cd231", "container_byte_span": {"end": 317111, "start": 315098}, "container_hash": "sha256:c301cf74a2dd2305f3d1af83a4e72e18582d3c42daab021c29963eac16107da4"}], "ordinal": 1, "owner_label": "sites-section-2-category", "owner_tag": "04I9", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14"}, "policy_hash": "sha256:7b11f07bb8ea599d6bc0f5696ba57ca1744aecf03c9a9d0b0ec9fb902c138757", "source_label": "sites-section-2-category", "usage": "quad-connector", "usage_source": {"after": "\\quad", "before": "\\quad", "environments": []}}, "command": "text", "policy_entry": "sites-or", "slot_byte_span": {"end": 114, "start": 112}, "slot_id": "math/0001/text/0001", "source": "or"}], "source": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nf'_*f_*\\mathcal{F}\n\\ar[r]^{f'_*t} &\nf'_*g_*\\mathcal{F}\n\\ar[r]^s &\ng'_*g_*\\mathcal{F}\n}\n\\quad\\text{or}\\quad\n\\xymatrix{\nf'_*f_*\\mathcal{F}\n\\ar[r]^s &\ng'_*f_*\\mathcal{F}\n\\ar[r]^{g'_*t} &\ng'_*g_*\\mathcal{F}\n}\n$$", "source_byte_span": {"end": 1737, "start": 1516}, "source_hash": "sha256:9eb2a411bff5c4618e1fd5eab6557f146ba07fb0ab9e684702050b0ea27c5739"}], "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04I9", "placeholders": {"MATHSEG_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nf'_*f_*\\mathcal{F}\n\\ar[r]^{f'_*t} &\nf'_*g_*\\mathcal{F}\n\\ar[r]^s &\ng'_*g_*\\mathcal{F}\n}\n\\quad\\text{", "MATHSEG_0002": "}\\quad\n\\xymatrix{\nf'_*f_*\\mathcal{F}\n\\ar[r]^s &\ng'_*f_*\\mathcal{F}\n\\ar[r]^{g'_*t} &\ng'_*g_*\\mathcal{F}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0001": "$t$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})\n\\rrtwocell^f_g{t}\n&\n&\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{D})\n}\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$f^{-1}$", "MATH_0004": "$f_*$", "MATH_0005": "$g^{-1}$", "MATH_0006": "$g_*$", "MATH_0007": "$t$", "MATH_0008": "$t : g^{-1} \\to f^{-1}$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Mor_{\\Sh(\\mathcal{D})}(\\mathcal{G}, f_*\\mathcal{F})\n\\ar[d]_{t \\circ -} \\ar@{=}[r] &\n\\Mor_{\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})}(f^{-1}\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F})\n\\ar[d]^{- \\circ t}\n\\\\\n\\Mor_{\\Sh(\\mathcal{D})}(\\mathcal{G}, g_*\\mathcal{F})\n\\ar@{=}[r] &\n\\Mor_{\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})}(g^{-1}\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F})\n}\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})\n\\rtwocell^f_g{t}\n&\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{D})\n\\rtwocell^{f'}_{g'}{s}\n&\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{E})\n}\n$$", "MATH_0011": "$s \\star t$", "MATH_0012": "$s \\star t$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-morphism-topoi-big}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{categories-section-2-categories}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{definition-topos}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{categories-definition-horizontal-composition}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{categories-section-formal-cat-cat}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{categories-lemma-properties-2-cat-cats}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8db587fa4bd1b67867b7d0b3c09fe9c39547847e9aee06f628af87dbca76793a", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:229e40ef6c8388c3795a48b40596e473ebbcc49db58d69a798b452121ce6b608", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cbe9a34b145c3211a725de4ef50909c3b08154caf1459a6c5313d39b85582073", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nPictorially we sometimes represent <MATH_0001> as follows:\n<MATH_0002>\nNote that since <MATH_0003> is adjoint to <MATH_0004> and\n<MATH_0005> is adjoint to <MATH_0006> we see that <MATH_0007> induces also\na transformation of functors\n<MATH_0008> (usually denoted by the same symbol)\nuniquely characterized by the condition that the diagram\n<MATH_0009>\ncommutes. Because of set theoretic difficulties (see\nRemark <REF_0001>)\nwe do not obtain a 2-category of topoi. But we can still define\nhorizontal and vertical composition and show that the axioms of a strict\n2-category listed in\nCategories, Section <REF_0002>\nhold.\nNamely, vertical composition of 2-morphisms is clear (just compose\ntransformations of functors), composition of 1-morphisms has been\ndefined in\nDefinition <REF_0003>,\nand horizontal composition of\n<MATH_0010>\nis defined by the transformation of functors <MATH_0011>\nintroduced in\nCategories, Definition <REF_0004>.\nExplicitly, <MATH_0012> is given by\n<MATHSEG_0001>or<MATHSEG_0002>\n(these maps are equal). Since these definitions agree with the ones in\nCategories, Section <REF_0005>\nit follows from\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0006>\nthat the axioms of a strict 2-category hold with these definitions.\n\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:40fc31189fed5d239d14e1d03cb9380360ba9e4b325e759cf6b533b6d08af3df", "unit_id": "tag:04I9:prose-0002"}
